    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Great Ferns Provincial Park\"\nsubtitle: \"Permanent plot · Grande Terre, New Caledonia\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-057a0404e0f323f4f6cd\" style=\"width:100%;height:367px;\" class=\"leaflet html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-057a0404e0f323f4f6cd\">{\"x\":{\"options\":{\"minZoom\":3,\"crs\":{\"crsClass\":\"L.CRS.EPSG3857\",\"code\":null,\"proj4def\":null,\"projectedBounds\":null,\"options\":{}}},\"calls\":[{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.WorldGrayCanvas\",null,\"Map\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addProviderTiles\",\"args\":[\"Esri.WorldImagery\",null,\"Satellite\",{\"errorTileUrl\":\"\",\"noWrap\":false,\"detectRetina\":false}]},{\"method\":\"addCircleMarkers\",\"args\":[[-20.727398,-22.10677311,-21.6119184,-19.385234,-7.88488,-18.077995],[167.090406,166.68812588,165.7468984,169.294602,157.127126,178.430887],7,null,null,{\"interactive\":true,\"className\":\"\",\"stroke\":true,\"color\":\"#16262B\",\"weight\":1,\"opacity\":0.5,\"fill\":true,\"fillColor\":\"#C98A1B\",\"fillOpacity\":0.6},null,null,[\"<b>Siloam<\\/b><br>Lifou, New Caledonia<br><a href='../plots/siloam.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Blue River Provincial Park<\\/b><br>Grande Terre, New Caledonia<br><a href='../plots/blue-river.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Great Ferns Provincial Park<\\/b><br>Grande Terre, New Caledonia<br><a href='../plots/great-ferns.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Nusumetu<\\/b><br>Tanna, Vanuatu<br><a href='../plots/nusumetu.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Poitete<\\/b><br>Kolombangara, Solomon Islands<br><a href='../plots/poitete.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\",\"<b>Vago<\\/b><br>Viti Levu, Fiji<br><a href='../plots/vago.html'>More &rarr;<\\/a>\"],null,null,{\"interactive\":false,\"permanent\":false,\"direction\":\"auto\",\"opacity\":1,\"offset\":[0,0],\"textsize\":\"10px\",\"textOnly\":false,\"className\":\"\",\"sticky\":true},null]},{\"method\":\"addLayersControl\",\"args\":[[\"Map\",\"Satellite\"],[],{\"collapsed\":false,\"autoZIndex\":true,\"position\":\"topright\"}]},{\"method\":\"addLegend\",\"args\":[{\"colors\":[\"#C98A1B\"],\"labels\":[\"Permanent plots\"],\"na_color\":null,\"na_label\":\"NA\",\"opacity\":1,\"position\":\"bottomleft\",\"type\":\"unknown\",\"title\":null,\"extra\":null,\"layerId\":null,\"className\":\"info legend\",\"group\":null}]}],\"limits\":{\"lat\":[-22.10677311,-7.88488],\"lng\":[157.127126,178.430887]},\"setView\":[[-21.6119184,165.7468984],9,[]]},\"evals\":[],\"jsHooks\":[]}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|                       |                                                                                                                         |\n|:----------------------|:------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n|Country                |New Caledonia                                                                                                            |\n|Island                 |Grande Terre                                                                                                             |\n|Latitude               |-21.6119                                                                                                                 |\n|Longitude              |165.7469                                                                                                                 |\n|Elevation (approx.)    |380 m                                                                                                                    |\n|Substrate              |Volcano-sedimentary (schists)                                                                                            |\n|Established            |September 2025                                                                                                           |\n|Principal investigator |Thomas Ibanez (Research Fellow, UMR AMAP, French National Research Institute for Sustainable Development, New Caledonia) |\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Description\n\nThe Great Ferns permanent plot lies in the Great Ferns Provincial Park, on a gentle slope with volcano-sedimentary soils in the centre of the island of Grande Terre. The park is managed by the South Province. The plot was set up in September 2025 at about 380 m elevation and resurveyed in September 2026. The forest was logged until the 1970s and has been protected since 2008. It shows signs of disturbance by introduced deer (*Rusa timorensis*).\n\nThe most abundant tree species are *Xylopia vieillardii* (Annonaceae), *Diospyros samoensis* (Ebenaceae) and *Calophyllum caledonicum* (Calophyllaceae). The largest tree is an *Agathis moorei* (Araucariaceae) and the tallest is a *Planchonella sphaerocarpa* (Sapotaceae).\n\n## Field team\n\nDavid Bruy, Celine Chambret, Julie Dibon, Nathan Eltabet, Alex Greene, Patrick Heuret, Thomas Ibanez, Chrystelle Nigote and Ghislain Vieilledent.\n\n[← All permanent plots](../plots.qmd) · [Network map](../index.qmd)\n",
